2025-01-29 Gunjan Poshiya<gunjan.poshiya@stl.tech> 
	* NEWS
	* Jira ID :  
	* Previous Commit ID : 5c02248b 
	* Version : Dev
	* Laravel & ReactJs :  Created API for Ticket report and SLA report
	with graphs, Pagination, Filters and listing view and CSV export.
	Key functionalities of the SLAReport component include:

	Date Range Filters: Users can select a start and end date for querying SLA data.
	User and Priority Filters: Allows filtering by user and priority level (Critical, High, Medium, Low, Normal).
	SLA Compliance Filter: Enables filtering tickets based on SLA compliance (Yes/No).
	Dynamic Data Fetching: Data is fetched dynamically using Axios based on the selected filters.
	Graph View: Provides a graphical view (pie and bar charts) summarizing SLA compliance, ticket counts by priority, category, and incident.
	Table View: Displays detailed ticket data in a table with pagination support.
	CSV Export: Users can download the report in CSV format for further analysis.
	Pagination: Supports pagination with configurable items per page.
	User Dropdown: Fetches and displays a list of users to filter by user.
	SLA Compliance Calculation: Tracks the number of compliant vs non-compliant tickets.

	The user should be able to toggle between graph and table views.
	The user should be able to download the report in CSV format.
	The pagination controls should function properly, allowing users to navigate through large datasets.
	The user should be able to filter data and immediately view the updated report.

