	The SLA Settings CRUD API allows users to manage SLA configurations, 
	including defining working hours, off days, holidays, and 
	response/resolve targets. Users can create, read, update, and 
	delete SLA settings, with each SLA entry identified by a unique 'name'. 
	The API supports associating off days, holidays, and service level targets (
	such as response and resolution times) to specific SLA configurations, 
	ensuring comprehensive management of SLA requirements. All operations 
	are fully integrated with relational tables for off days, holidays, 
	and service level targets, ensuring data integrity through foreign key relationships.

