2024-12-13 Gunjan Poshiya<gunjan.poshiya@stl.tech> 
	* NEWS
	* Jira ID :
	* Previous Commit ID : 
	* Version : Dev
	* React & Laravel : 
	    SuperAdmin License Generation

	 Purpose: The License Generator allows the creation of SuperAdmin licenses.
	How it Works:
	Granting full access to the system and the ability to manage other tenant users.
	 The SuperAdmin license has a defined expiration date, and its validity is essential for system access. If the SuperAdmin license expires, all operations tied to SuperAdmin privileges will cease to function.

	Tenant SuperAdmin License Management
	If the SuperAdmin has a license that allows 100 Enterprise, the SuperAdmin can generate up to 100 licenses for Tenant. The number of licenses created cannot exceed the total available under the SuperAdmin’s license.
	License Expiry & User Access:
	If the SuperAdmin license expires, Tenant users will no longer be able to log in or access the system.
	 The expiration of the SuperAdmin license will trigger the expiration of all associated tenant licenses, as access rights are bound by the validity of the SuperAdmin’s license.

	License Usage Flow
	The SuperAdmin creates individual licenses for Tenant.
	 The number of Tenant licenses cannot exceed the number granted by the SuperAdmin.
	License validity:
	Each Tenant user’s access is valid as long as the SuperAdmin’s license remains active.
	If the SuperAdmin’s license expires, all Tenant user licenses become inactive, and users will be unable to log in to the system.

	Key Considerations
	License Renewal:
	 The SuperAdmin must renew their license before it expires to ensure continued access for both themselves and the Tenant users.
	If the SuperAdmin’s license expires, the Tenant users lose access, regardless of their individual license status.
	License Validation:
	The system should continuously validate that the SuperAdmin license is active before allowing access for Tenant users.
	
